func isPalindrome(_ input: String) -> Bool {
    let alphanumericInput = input.lowercased().components(separatedBy: CharacterSet.alphanumerics.inverted).joined()
    return alphanumericInput == String(alphanumericInput.reversed())
}

// Test cases
assert(isPalindrome("racecar") == true)
assert(isPalindrome("hello") == false)
assert(isPalindrome("A man a plan a canal Panama") == true)
```

The `isPalindrome` function first converts the input string to lowercase and removes non-alphanumeric characters. Then, it checks if the resulting string is equal to its reverse, returning `true` if they match and `false` otherwise. The provided test cases validate the correctness of the function.

